\p
\v 1 In¦376324 the eighth¦376325 month¦376324 of the second year¦376326 of¦376328 \add the reign of Persian King\add* Dareyavesh¦376328 \add !(Darius¦376328)\add*, Yahweh¦376332 \add ≈spoke through\add* the prophet¦376342 Zekaryah¦376335 (\add Zechariah,\add* son of Iddo's¦376341 son Berekyah¦376338) saying¦376343,\x + \xo 1:1: \xt Ezr 4:24–5:1; 6:14.\x*
\v 2 “Yahweh¦376346 was¦376345 very angry¦376345 with your¦376349 ancestors¦376349,
\v 3 \add ≈so¦376354\add* tell¦376352 \add this to\add* \add @the¦376360 people¦376360\add*: Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376356 says¦376355 \add ≈that if you all turn back\add* to¦376359 me¦376359, I'll¦376363 return¦376363 to¦376364 you.
\v 4 Don't¦376369 be¦376371 like¦376372 your ancestors¦376372 who'd been told¦376374 by the¦376377 prophets¦376377 that Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376400 wanted them¦376376 to¦376379 abandon \add ≈all\add* their evil¦376387 practices, \add ≈but¦376388\add* they¦376393 wouldn't listen¦376393 or pay¦376396 attention¦376396. That is Yahweh's¦376382 declaration¦376398.
\p
\v 5 “\add So\add* where¦376403 are¦376405 you ancestors¦376402 and¦376406 the¦376406 prophets¦376406 \add now\add*? Do¦376408 they¦376405 live¦376408 forever¦376407?
\v 6 But¦376413 your¦376422 ancestors¦376422 \add ≈didn't¦376420 obey\add* my words¦376412 and¦376413 my¦376413 decrees that¦376414 I¦376415 commanded¦376415 \add through\add* my servants¦376418 the¦376419 prophets¦376419, but¦376410 they¦376424 \add eventually\add* repented¦376423 and¦376424 said¦376424, ‘Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376427 has¦376434 done¦376434 to¦376430 us¦376430 just¦376425 what our¦376431 ways¦376431 and¦376432 actions¦376432 deserved.’ ”
\s1 Yahweh's compassion for Yerushalem
\rem /s1 First Vision: The Horsemen; Eight visions with their interpretations; The Man Among the Myrtle Trees; A Man among the Myrtle Trees; The Prophet's Vision of the Horses
