\v 7 \add ≈About three months¦376444 later\add*, Yahweh¦376455 \add ≈spoke again through\add* the¦376447 prophet¦376465 Zekaryah¦376458 (\add Zechariah\add* son¦376459 of¦376459 Iddo's¦376464 son Berekyah¦376461) saying¦376466,
\v 8 “I \add ≈had a vision\add* in the¦376470 night¦376470, and \add ≈was surprised to see¦376468\add* a man¦376473 riding¦376474 on¦376484 a red horse¦376477,\x + \xo 1:8a: \xt Rev 6:4.\x* and¦376479 then he¦376479 was¦376480 standing¦376480 among¦376481 the¦376482 myrtle¦376482 trees¦376482 that¦376483 are¦376484 in¦376484 the valley, and¦376485 behind¦376485 him¦376485 there were¦376485 red¦376487, reddish-brown, and¦376489 white¦376489 horses¦376486.”\x + \xo 1:8b: \xt Rev 6:2.\x*
\v 9 I¦376501 \add ≈asked¦376491\add*, “What¦376492 are¦376494 these¦376494 things, my¦376495 master¦376495?”
\p Then¦376491 \add ≈that¦376499\add* \add heavenly\add* messenger¦376498 who¦376499 talked¦376499 with¦376500 me told¦376491 me, “I'll¦376502 show¦376502 you¦376502 what¦376503 those¦376494 things are¦376506.”
\p
\v 10 Then¦376508 the¦376509 man¦376509 who¦376510 stood¦376510 among¦376511 the¦376513 myrtle¦376513 trees¦376513 answered¦376508 and¦376515 said¦376515, “Those¦376518 are¦376517 the ones that Yahweh¦376519 has¦376518 sent¦376518 out to¦376520 roam throughout the¦376521 world¦376521.”
\p
\v 11 They¦376523 answered¦376523 Yahweh's¦376527 messenger¦376526 who¦376528 stood¦376528 among¦376529 the¦376530 myrtle¦376530 trees¦376530, telling¦376531 him, “We've¦376534 been roaming throughout the world, and see¦376534, the whole¦376535 world sits¦376538 \add ≈contentedly\add* and¦376539 is¦376539 at peace¦376539.”
\p
\v 12 “Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376546,” Yahweh's¦376544 messenger¦376542 \add ≈asked¦376545\add*, “how long \add ≈before\add* you show compassion¦376554 to Yerushalem¦376557 and¦376541 to the cities¦376559 of¦376559 Yehudah¦376560 \add !(Judah¦376560)\add*, which¦376561 you've¦376554 been¦376562 angry¦376562 with for the past seventy¦376564 years¦376565?”
\p
\v 13 Then¦376567 that¦376572 messenger¦376571 who'd talked¦376572 with¦376573 me¦376573 was¦376572 answered¦376567 by Yahweh¦376568 with kind and¦376567 comforting¦376577 words¦376574,
\v 14 and¦376579 that¦376582 messenger¦376581 told¦376579 me¦376583, “Call out and say¦376585, ‘Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376588 says¦376587 this: I've been¦376590 \add ≈very\add* jealous¦376590 for¦376591 Yerushalem¦376591 and¦376592 for¦376592 Tsiyyon¦376592 \add !(Zion¦376592)\add*.
\v 15 I'm¦376598 very angry¦376599 with the¦376602 countries¦376602 that¦376604 are at¦376603 ease¦376603—I¦376605 was¦376606 only a little¦376607 angry with them, \add ≈but¦376596\add* they¦376608 made the disaster¦376610 worse.
\v 16 Therefore Yahweh says¦376615: I¦376617 \add ≈will show mercy¦376619\add* Yerushalem¦376618 \add ≈again\add*. My¦376620 residence will¦376621 be¦376621 built¦376621 within her, and¦376626 the¦376623 measuring¦376626 line will¦376628 be¦376628 stretched¦376628 out¦376628 over¦376629 her. That's what Commander-in-chief Yahweh declares¦376623.
\p
\v 17 “Again¦376633, call out and say¦376636, ‘Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦376639 says¦376638 this: My¦376646 cities¦376643 will¦376642 once again overflow¦376642 with¦376653 goodness¦376644, and¦376645 \add *I¦376646\add* will¦376645 again comfort¦376645 Tsiyyon¦376650 and¦376651 choose¦376651 Yerushalem¦376653.’ ”
\s1 The vision of the four horns
\rem /s1 The Vision of the Horns; Four Horns and Four Blacksmiths; Four Horns and Four Craftsmen; Second Vision: The Horns and the Smiths
\p
\v 18 Then I \add ≈looked up\add* and wow, I saw four horns.
\v 19 I \add ≈asked\add* the messenger who'd talked with me, “What are those?”
\p “Those are the horns that have scattered Yehudah, Yisrael, and Yerushalem.” he \add ≈answered\add*.
\p
\v 20 Then Yahweh showed me four craftsmen
\v 21 and I \add ≈asked\add*, “What are those people coming to do?”
\p “Those horns are \add the nations\add* that scattered Yehudah so that \add ≈everyone went into hiding\add*,” he \add ≈answered\add*, “But the blacksmiths have come to terrify \add the horns\add*—to \add ≈amputate\add* the horns of the nations that \add ≈attacked\add* Yehudah, scattering \add @the people\add*.”
\c 2
\s1 The vision of Yerushalem expanded
\rem /s1 Third Vision: The Man with a Measuring Line; A Man With a Measuring Line; The Vision of the Measuring Line; Future Prosperity of Jerusalem
\p
\v 1 Then I \add ≈looked¦376661 up¦376657\add*, and¦376657 wow, I saw¦376661 a man \add ≈holding\add* a measuring line\f + \fr 2:1 \ft The modern equivalent would be a tape measure.\f*
\v 2 and¦376667 I¦376667 asked¦376667 him, “Where are¦376675 you going?”
\p “To¦376677 measure Yerushalem¦376688,” he¦376676 \add ≈replied¦376667\add*, “and¦376676 to¦376677 determine its width and¦376688 length.”
\p
\v 3 Then¦376694 \add ≈to my surprise\add*, the messenger who'd talked with me¦376693 went away and¦376693 another messenger went out to meet him
\v 4 and¦376699 told¦376699 him, “Run and¦376704 speak¦376714 to¦376705 that¦376708 young man¦376716, saying¦376699: Yerushalem \add ≈won't¦376717 need city walls\add* because \add ≈there'll be so many\add* people¦376716 and¦376721 animals within it¦376736.
\v 5 Yahweh declares that he'll become a wall of¦376741 fire around it and¦376742 will become the splendour in¦376746 the middle of it.
\s1 Yahweh commands the exiles to go home
