\p
\v 6 Then¦377037 \add *he¦377037\add* told¦377041 Yehoshua¦377040,
\v 7 “Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦377046 says¦377045: If¦377048 you'll¦377051 \add ≈follow my instructions\add* and obey my rules, then you can govern¦377060 my \add ≈temple¦377063\add* and¦377064 guard¦377065 my courtyards¦377068, because I'll¦377069 allow you to¦377070 walk¦377051 among¦377072 these¦377074 who¦377073 are¦377073 standing¦377073 here.
\v 8 Please¦377078 listen, Yehoshua¦377079 the high¦377082 priest¦377081, \add ≈as well as\add* your¦377086 companions¦377084 sitting¦377085 in front¦377086 of¦377084 you¦377083. Those these men¦377089 are¦377089 a sign¦377090, because¦377087 I¦377094 myself will¦377089 bring¦377095 out my¦377098 servant¦377098 ‘the branch¦377099’.\x + \xo 3:8: \xt Jer 23:5; 33:15; Zech 6:12.\x*
\v 9 Now look at the¦377104 stone¦377104 that¦377105 I've¦377106 placed¦377106 in front¦377107 of¦377107 Yehoshua¦377108—a single¦377112 stone with seven¦377113 \add ≈faces¦377107\add* \add cut on it\add*. Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦377119 declares¦377118 that I will engrave¦377116 an inscription¦377117 on it, and¦377121 I will¦377121 remove¦377121 the sin from this land¦377125 in¦377128 one¦377129 day¦377128.
\v 10 Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦377134 declares¦377133 that in that day¦377131, each¦377137 man¦377137 will¦377136 invite¦377136 his neighbour¦377138 to¦377139 sit under¦377141 his grapevine¦377142 or under¦377145 his fig¦377146 tree¦377146.”\x + \xo 3:10: \xt Mic 4:4.\x*
\c 4
